pySMESH: Cartesian_3D with viscous layers marks the sub-meshes of the meshed solids computed
(SMESH V9_16_0; applies after StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D_offset_mesh_leak.patch).

Defect: after a successful compute with viscous layers, an EDGE or VERTEX sub-mesh with no
element of its own reads as not computed, so the compute is reported as failed on it with no
message although the mesh is complete.

Symptom: a cylinder (the seam EDGE), a sphere (the seam and the poles), a block with a bore
(the bore's seam), layers on every face: complete meshes, each reported as failed on those
sub-shapes.

Root cause: the plain path marks every sub-mesh of each solid computed after it makes the
volumes (setSubmeshesComputed, StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx:229, :390-395). The viscous path
runs the plain path on the offset mesh only (:144-165), so the marks land on the offset mesh
and not on the target.

Change, in StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx only: after MakeViscousLayers succeeds, the target's
sub-meshes are marked as the plain path marks them.

Not changed: a failed compute, and the plain path.
diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx
@@ -165,7 +165,15 @@
     if ( ! this->Compute( *offsetMesh, offsetShape ))
       return false;
 
-    return builder.MakeViscousLayers( *offsetMesh, theMesh, theShape, &_computeCanceled );
+    if ( !builder.MakeViscousLayers( *offsetMesh, theMesh, theShape, &_computeCanceled ))
+      return false;
+
+    // pySMESH: the layers complete the mesh of every solid, but only the offset mesh had
+    // its sub-meshes marked computed (by the inner call); an EDGE or VERTEX with no
+    // element of its own (a seam, a pole) then read as failed. Mark them as the plain path
+    // does.
+    setSubmeshesComputed( theMesh, theShape );
+    return true;
   }
 
